course: dictionary
lesson: 8483
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word sand can name a material, a place, or a job. Read the words around it first.
explain: «Ostriches do not bury their heads in the sand; to hide they lie flat with their necks along the ground.» Here sand means the grains on the ground, because the sentence is about hiding on the ground, not about a beach or a job.
explain: «Sands» with an s means a large area of sand, such as a beach or a desert. Sand can also be a verb, an action word: to sand wood is to rub it with sandpaper until it is smooth. Ask yourself: is it a thing, a place, or something someone does?
fact: Sand is tiny grains of rock and shell, found on beaches and in deserts.
fact: Sand is made slowly when water and wind break rocks and shells into tiny pieces. This is called weathering.
fact: «Sands» means a large area of sand, like the sands of a beach.
fact: As a verb, «sand» means to rub wood with sandpaper to make it smooth.
fact: Glass is made by melting sand, so sand is an important material in everyday life.
exercise: «Ostriches do not bury their heads in the sand.» What does sand mean here? | A castle built for play | A large sandy beach | To rub wood until it is smooth | *Tiny grains of rock and shell
exercise: Mia says, «We played on the sands all afternoon.» What does sands mean here? | To rub something smooth with paper | A tall sandcastle tower | Tiny grains of rock and shell | *A large area of sand, like a beach
exercise: Dad says, «Sand the table before you paint it.» What does sand mean in this sentence? | To melt into glass | *To rub with sandpaper to make it smooth | A place where animals live | Grains of rock on a beach
test: Glass is made by melting what? | Ice | Feathers | Wood | *Sand
test: In «I will sand the chair this afternoon», what does sand mean? | *To rub the chair with sandpaper to make it smooth | A large beach by the chair | Tiny grains of rock on the chair | A small castle made for play
exam: Which of these is a safe way to play with sand? | *Build a sandcastle, but do not dig a deep hole that could collapse | Throw handfuls of sand at your friends | Lie on hot sand with bare feet all day | Dig a deep hole and jump into it
